Subject: FMCSA Motor Carrier Address Clusters – Indicators of Potential Authority Misuse / Shell Activity

To the Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration and relevant enforcement contacts,

Attached please find a curated dataset of ${cluster_count} address clusters involving FMCSA-registered motor carriers, representing over ${"{:,}".format(total_carriers)} individual USDOT authorities. These clusters were identified through analysis of IRS Form 990 data cross-referenced with FMCSA registration records and then manually reviewed using publicly available mapping tools.

Key patterns observed include:
- Frequent use of PO Boxes or virtual/mailbox services listed as physical addresses
- High concentrations of inactive authority at single locations with minimal apparent operational footprint
- Multiple carriers listing the same address with characteristics consistent with front companies or authority stacking

The attached files include both cluster-level summaries and carrier-level detail to facilitate efficient review.

This information is provided in good faith to assist enforcement and compliance efforts. I am available to provide additional context, methodology details, or supporting data upon request.

